threads.body:
@copilot Simplify the existing Vert.x 5 HTTP client retention fix in this PR. Update this PR directly at its verified head `open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation:copilot/fix-vertx-http-client-fallback`, not a separate PR. Keep the branch GitHub Copilot cloud agent assigns, including any platform-assigned follow-up branch; do not rename it or create a replacement branch.

In the `vertx-http-client-5.0/javaagent` module, store the existing `io.vertx.core.net.SocketAddress` from `connection.remoteAddress()` directly in the response `VirtualField` instead of allocating and populating an `AddressAndPort` per response. Vert.x 5.0.0's built-in `SocketAddressImpl` stores only address data and has no reference to the connection or response; `ConnectionBase` returns that value for the standard transports. Keep capturing the address during response construction in `HttpClientResponseImplInstrumentation`. In `Vertx5HttpAttributesGetter`, read `hostAddress()` and `port()` from the stored address, preserving the existing null/absent behavior and emitted values. Do not retain the live `HttpConnection` in the field or add another wrapper, cast, or allocation.

Keep the change scoped to this simplification. Leave unrelated telemetry and lifecycle handling alone. Do not restore `Vertx5HttpAttributesGetterTest` or its Gradle wiring; use the existing Vert.x 5 HTTP client tests for targeted validation.

